{"name":"Eternity","hex":"#2d2f28","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eternity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Existence without end, infinite time.","Existence outside of time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eternity","blocks":[{"text":"Eternity, also sempiternity or forever, or perpetuity, is time with no end, i.e. infinite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternity"},{"title":"Eternity (2025 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Eternity is a 2025 American fantasy romantic comedy film directed by David Freyne, who co-wrote the film with Pat Cunnane. The film stars Elizabeth Olsen as a woman forced to choose whom to spend eternity with in the afterlife: her second husband of 65 years, played by Miles Teller, or her first husband who died young, portrayed by Callum Turner. Da'Vine Joy Randolph, John Early, and Olga Merediz appear in supporting roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6b/Eternity_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternity_(2025_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Jacopo_da_Sellaio_-_Triumph_of_Eternity_-_1485-90.jpg/250px-Jacopo_da_Sellaio_-_Triumph_of_Eternity_-_1485-90.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Jacopo_da_Sellaio_-_Triumph_of_Eternity_-_1485-90.jpg/500px-Jacopo_da_Sellaio_-_Triumph_of_Eternity_-_1485-90.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Jacopo_da_Sellaio_-_Triumph_of_Eternity_-_1485-90.jpg/250px-Jacopo_da_S